{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Moses grew up and went out to his brothers</b> — that he grew and became a man, for at first it says, \"And the child grew\" (Exodus 2:10), meaning he grew before he needed to be weaned, and then she brought him to Pharaoh's daughter and he became a son to her, for he would stand before kings, and afterward he grew and became a man of understanding:" "And the sense of <b>and he went out to his brothers</b> is that they told him that he was a Jew, and he desired to see them because they were his brothers. And behold, he looked upon their burdens and their toil and could not endure it, and therefore he killed the Egyptian who was striking the oppressed one:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:26.593696221Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}